lograms), Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "28 July 2021"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/465"} "Nippon Budokan, Chiyoda, Tokyo"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/18001088"} "33 from 33 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "The Japanese winning streak in the men’s events came to a halt in the middleweight class. " [:a {:href "/athletes/144676"} "Shoichiro Mukai"] " did not come as one of the favourites and lost his second bout against Hungarian " [:a {:href "/athletes/134371"} "Krisztián Tóth"] " by Ippon (full point). After top seed and 2021 world champion " [:a {:href "/athletes/142554"} "Nikoloz Sherazadishvili"] ", representing Spain, was defeated in the quarter-final, the way was paved for another Georgian, " [:a {:href "/athletes/143218"} "Lasha Bekauri"] ". Bekauri competed as a junior until 2019 and took the European title in 2021. In Tokyo, he scored victories over Uzbek " [:a {:href "/athletes/147542"} "Davlat Bobonov"] ", 2014 Youth Olympic Games double gold medallist " [:a {:href "/athletes/2104238"} "Mikhail Igolnikov"] ", representing the Russian Olympic Committee, and, in the final, German policeman " [:a {:href "/athletes/143450"} "Eduard Trippel"] ". Bobonov was penalized for a banned head dive, giving his opponent Bekauri an Ippon. The fight against Igolnikov was eventually decided by Waza-ari (half point) in his favour, although Bekauri had already two Shidos (penalties) on his account."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In the final, Bekauri scored a Waza-ari for a Tsurikomi-goshi after 1:30 min and held on to his lead until the end of the fight for gold. Seventh seed Trippel not only defeated the 2017 Serbian world champion " [:a {:href "/athletes/2104311"} "Nemanja Majdov"] ", but also sent fourth seed, and 2010 Youth Olympic Games medallist, Tóth into the repêchage. Trippel had contracted COVID-19 during a training camp in Georgia but the symptoms were mild and he was able to take up training immediately after being released from quarantine. Bronze medals went to Bobonov and Tóth."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/143218"} "Lasha Bekauri"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GEO"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GEO.png"}] "GEO"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/143450"} "Eduard Trippel"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GER.png"}] "GER"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "=3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/147542"} "Davlat Bobonov"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/UZB"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/UZB.png"}] "UZB"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "=3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/134371"} "Krisztián Tóth"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/HUN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/HUN.png"}] "HUN"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "=5"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/135877"} "Mihael Žgank"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/TUR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/TUR.png"}] "TUR"]] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]]